  "summary": "DERIVED reconstruction of 26 runtime helper functions. Cluster A (network teardown): 0x0057FBE0 drains two mutex-protected linked lists, runs a subsystem cleanup helper, invokes the vtable+48 virtual cleanup, and conditionally calls WSACleanup gated on the winsockInitialized flag at this+0xA74. Cluster B (multi-block bitfield): 0x00586800 encodes four bitfield blocks into a bitmap array using a metadata table at this+0x1C, 0x00586AA0 resets the same state, and 0x00586F40 builds entry-count-clipped masks; they share the bitmap base at this+0x14 and index fields at this+0x34..0x44, and use 0x00585E80 as the bit-index-to-mask utility. Cluster C (stream I/O): 0x00587CA0, 0x00587D02, 0x00587F64, 0x00588678, 0x005887B1 and 0x0058ACE6 all serialize through StreamBufferLockViaCriticalSection (0x0058C1B1) / AddressRangeCriticalSectionLeave (0x0058C203), forming a single locked file/stream contract. Cluster D (string helpers): bounded copy (0x00587DD0), bounded compare (0x00588640), delimiter tokenizer with TLS scan state (0x005897CA), locale/ASCII uppercase (0x00589901), masked stream read (0x0058801D), formatting wrappers (0x005887B1, 0x0058969D). Cluster E (Win32/D3D/Winsock surface): directory create (0x00589671), read-only toggle (0x0058BA36), import thunks WSAStartup (0x0059869C) and Direct3DCreate8 (0x0059B250), plus small helpers 0x00587B3E, 0x00587DB0, 0x00587F59, 0x00595058 and the no-op SEH stub 0x0058A5D8. No CONFIRMED claim is made about original source names or class layout.",
